KORD: SUPABASE SECURITY AND BACKEND INTEGRITY AUDIT & REPAIR
You are working on the existing Kord web application repository.
Your task is to conduct a thorough audit and repair of the Supabase database security, learning progression logic, assessment system, and frontend database integration.
This is an existing project. You are not starting from scratch.
Project context
Kord is a skill-development platform built with:
Vanilla JavaScript, HTML and CSS.
Supabase for authentication, PostgreSQL database, Row Level Security (RLS), database functions and storage.
An existing repository architecture and frontend implementation.
Kord's learning model is:
Learn → Understand → Demonstrate
Learners should:
Learn through structured courses, lessons and resources.
Demonstrate understanding through quizzes and assessments.
Demonstrate practical ability through challenges and evidence submissions.
Practical demonstration must not be replaced by simply passing a multiple-choice quiz.
Critical project status
The Supabase project has been created, but the SQL files in this repository have NOT been deployed to Supabase.
Therefore:
Treat all existing SQL as proposed implementation, not verified production functionality.
Do not claim that any database functionality is currently working.
Do not assume the database schema has been deployed.
Do not delete existing implementation simply because it has not been deployed.
Do not invent database tables, policies, functions or frontend behavior without examining the actual repository.
